<figure class="checkpoint" aria-labelledby="r36-checkpoint-title">
 <p class="figure-title" id="r36-checkpoint-title">Figure 2 · The checkpoint record points backwards</p>
 <div class="log"><div class="old">Older WAL<br/><small>No longer needed for this local restart</small></div><div class="redo"><strong>Redo position</strong><br/>Start replay here</div><div class="during">Writes continue<br/><small>while dirty pages are written</small></div><div class="record"><strong>Checkpoint record</strong><br/>Remembers the redo position</div></div>
 <p class="backlink">Checkpoint record ← points back to the redo position</p>
 <figcaption>A conceptual log, read left to right; narrow screens stack it in that same order. The completed checkpoint establishes a safe restart position. It does not mean every page reflects the moment when the checkpoint record was inserted. Other retention needs, including archives and replicas, can still require older WAL.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>.checkpoint{border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);padding:1rem;margin:2rem 0;background:var(--color-surface-alt);font:.9rem/1.5 var(--font-sans)}.checkpoint .figure-title{margin:0 0 1rem;font-size:1.1rem}.log{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:.3rem}.log>div{padding:.65rem;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary)}.log .redo,.log .record{border:2px solid var(--color-accent)}.old{color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.backlink{color:var(--color-accent);margin:.8rem 0}figcaption{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}@media(max-width:600px){.log{grid-template-columns:1fr}.log>div+div:before{content:'↓ ';color:var(--color-accent)}}</style>
